{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792481391,"nonce":"Wq/aAmnwEEY5DkHdlr8P36Ab8zs=","title":"Embed: preserve floating-point arguments at promoted host entries","message":"A native TypeScript cross-tier regression calls score(number):number from the host. Interpreted score(3) returns 42; after Cranelift promotion score(5) returns 12 rather than 62. TieredRuntime::call_raw reaches call_native_with_signature, which bit-packs every argument into i64 and invokes an all-integer function prototype, placing floats in the wrong ABI register class. The shared interpreter already has checked mixed-scalar extern dispatch.\n\nReuse that typed dispatcher at the host entry boundary, reject unsupported signature shapes before calling, and preserve argument count/type validation and pointer/float return decoding. Exercise actual float argument values, mixed integer/float order, floating returns, pointers, and post-promotion TypeScript execution. This is a shared embed ABI fix, not a frontend workaround.","files":null}]}